      "id": "8e6f45c4-51d0-415a-91d3-fab13493d7a7",
      "name": "Enquiry form",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.formTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        -260,
        -180
      ],
      "webhookId": "0a8949a0-03e3-4726-ab49-fc8337a113e8"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// One shape for every channel. The form is only one door \u2014 email, SMS and phone\n// transcripts arrive via other triggers and are normalised to exactly this object,\n// so everything downstream reads the same fields regardless of where it came from.\n//\n// `raw` is never overwritten anywhere in the pipeline. Extraction can then be re-run\n// and compared later, which is what makes the prompt-version comparison possible.\nconst now = new Date().toISOString();\n\nreturn items.map((item, i) => {\n  const f = item.json;\n  return {\n    json: {\n      job_id: `JOB-${new Date().getFullYear()}-${String(Date.now()).slice(-4)}${i}`,\n      state: 'new',\n      created_at: now,\n      channel: f.channel ?? 'web-form',\n      raw: f.raw ?? '',\n      form_customer_name: f.customer_name ?? null,\n      form_email: f.email ?? null,\n      form_phone: f.phone ?? null,\n      form_address: f.address ?? null,\n      events: [],\n    },\n  };\n});"
      },
      "id": "1b49bdf4-8a9e-4960-aceb-3e09ba208f99",
      "name": "Normalise inbound",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -180
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "text": "={{ $json.raw }}",
        "schemaType": "manual",
        "inputSchema": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"customer_name\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"email\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"phone\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"locality\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"language\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"de\",\n        \"en\",\n        \"fr\",\n        \"it\",\n        \"unknown\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"job_type\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"described_scope\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"urgency\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"emergency\",\n        \"urgent\",\n        \"scheduled\",\n        \"no_rush\",\n        \"unknown\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"deadline\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"in_service_area\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"boolean\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"is_repeat_customer\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"missing_fields\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"extraction_confidence\": {\n      \"type\": \"number\"\n    },\n    \"disqualify_reason\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"language\",\n    \"urgency\",\n    \"missing_fields\",\n    \"extraction_confidence\"\n  ]\n}",
        "options": {
          "systemPromptTemplate": "You extract structured data from enquiry messages sent to a small tax and accounting advisory firm in canton St. Gallen, Switzerland. They arrive in German or English and are often incomplete.\n\nNever invent a value. If a field is not present, return null and name it in missing_fields. A plausible guess is worse than a null: a null gets asked about, a guess gets acted on.\n\nKeep described_scope in the language it was written in and set language accordingly.\n\nurgency is about consequence, not tone. A calm message can describe an emergency and an angry one can describe something trivial. For this business, treat as an emergency: Genuinely time-critical means a statutory or authority-set clock is already running and missing it forfeits a right or triggers a penalty that cannot be undone by working faster later. Concretely: an objection period against a tax assessment that expires within days, a payment or filing demand from the cantonal tax office or the Federal Tax Administration with a stated deadline, a notice of audit or of an ex-officio (discretionary) assessment, a debt-collection or bankruptcy notice, or a VAT or payroll filing whose deadline falls before the next working week. These escalate to a qualified human immediately and are never answered by an automated reply alone, because the reply itself can be read as advice. Deadline periods here are illustrative and must be verified against the actual notice.\n\nService area \u2014 Distance is a weak qualifier here: almost all of this work is done remotely from documents, so a client in Zurich or Chur is no harder to serve than one in Wittenbach and must not be refused on geography. What actually qualifies an enquiry is client type and entity type (private individual, sole proprietor, GmbH/AG, association), whether the subject matter sits inside the firm's competence and licensing, and whether the firm is free of conflict to act.\nIn: St. Gallen, Gossau, Wittenbach, Goldach, Rorschach, Herisau, Flawil, Arbon. Out: Geneva, Lugano, Sion, Lausanne. If a locality is stated but you do not recognise it, return null rather than guessing \u2014 a wrong false loses real work.\n\nextraction_confidence is your honest estimate that a human reading the same text would extract the same fields. Do not inflate it.\n\nIf no actionable engagement is described at all, set job_type null and give a disqualify_reason."
        }
      },
      "id": "c9cbbba5-fcf0-430f-864c-620f571d7e36",
      "name": "Extract enquiry fields",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.informationExtractor",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        220,
        -180
      ]
    },
