    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## The escalation branch\n\nThis is the only unconditional exit from the automated path in W1.\n\nGenuinely time-critical means a statutory or authority-set clock is already running and missing it forfeits a right or triggers a penalty that cannot be undone by working faster later. Concretely: an objection period against a tax assessment that expires within days, a payment or filing demand from the cantonal tax office or the Federal Tax Administration with a stated deadline, a notice of audit or of an ex-officio (discretionary) assessment, a debt-collection or bankruptcy notice, or a VAT or payroll filing whose deadline falls before the next working week. These escalate to a qualified human immediately and are never answered by an automated reply alone, because the reply itself can be read as advice. Deadline periods here are illustrative and must be verified against the actual notice.\n\nNone of that belongs in a pricing pipeline. If your triage ever routes one into the normal flow, **report it** \u2014 an automation that handles an emergency as routine admin is exactly the kind of boundary failure this thesis is about.",
        "width": 380,
        "height": 240,
        "color": 2
      },
